WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.560
Step 1 of 9. 179 debate transcripts from 1960 to 2024, split into 44,255 speaking turns.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.740
Step 2 of 9. One dot per debate: the share of words spoken by moderators and panellists.

3
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.340
Step 3 of 9. Switch the measure to words per candidate turn: turns have shortened since the 1960s.

4
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.600
Step 4 of 9. Select a dot to open a debate: Kennedy and Nixon in Chicago, 26 September 1960.

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.760
Step 5 of 9. The debate turn by turn: each block is one turn, as wide as it is long.

6
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.840
Step 6 of 9. Share of words, a stand-in for talk time, and the length of every turn by speaker.

7
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.260
Step 7 of 9. Back to the overview to jump 64 years ahead.

8
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:39.130
Step 8 of 9. Harris and Trump in Philadelphia, 10 September 2024.

9
00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:44.880
Step 9 of 9. Four times as many candidate turns, averaging 123 words where 1960 averaged 328.
